[CONTEXT 1] Green growth
    URL: https://unevenearth.org/2022/10/green-growth/
    PUBLISHED: Mon, 31 Oct 2022 00:00:19 +0000
    SOURCE TEXT:
    by Winne van Woerden â€œWe need to foster sources of economic growth consistent with resilient ecosystems .â€ â€œWe need to decouple economic growth from resource use .â€ In the midst of heated conversation about the ecological crisis, there always seems to be someone making these kinds of points. This is â€˜green growthâ€™ thinking. It is promoted by leading multilateral organisations and is assumed in national and international policymaking, including the European Green Deal, IPCC reports, the Paris Agreement and most recently in the USâ€™ Inflation Reduction Act. You are also likely to come across green growth in your private quarrels; for many, it has become common sense. The green growth p...

[CONTEXT 2] Growth mania is fueling dangerous advances in AI â€“ and its existential risks
    URL: https://www.resilience.org/stories/2026-07-09/growth-mania-is-fueling-dangerous-advances-in-ai-and-its-existential-risks/
    PUBLISHED: Thu, 09 Jul 2026 08:00:55 +0000
    SOURCE TEXT:
    AI risk represents the apex of growth mania, where a few tech elites gamble with humanityâ€™s future. They take these risks without our consent and without our interests in mind. The result could be humanity being replaced as Earthâ€™s most intelligent species by a silicon-based successor.

